LANGUAGE English
DEBUG OFF

BOOK DvmRescueBoy ORDERED KEEP LOOPED
    IF goal != goalRescueBoy THEN EXIT

    PAGE Page1
        BUTTON "Read the first page" AFTER "Table of Contents"

        PROLOG "The {c:QItemDVM} looks old and worn with time."

        TEXT "
            Table of Contents

            You open the book to the first page. It>s a table of contents. You
            quickly scan down to find the spell to open portals. On the inside
            cover, someone--probably {c:EventChosenInvestigator}>s father--
            scrawled a note that reads, <<Only my descendants will be able to
            read this book, and only at the appointed hour. I have seen to
            this.>> You glance at the table of contents and see <<Travel, page
            72.>>

            Gain 1 {clue} the first time you read this page.
        "
    END PAGE

    PAGE Page2
        PROLOG "
            The book seems to contain spells and rituals, and
            {c:EventChosenInvestigator} may have... abilities. The book is
            thick and should be examined carefully.
        "
        
        BUTTON "Turn to page 72" AFTER "Portal"

        TEXT "
            You flip through the pages finally find the <<Travel>> section on
            page 72. The first entry is for portals.

            Portals
            
            You read through an overview of the spell and skim past the opening
            ritual. Behind it is a closing ritual: how shut down a portal that
            has already been cast.
            
            There is a list of materials and artifacts needed. You note that
            closing a portal seems to use the same materials as opening one.
            The list includes a {c:QItemDagger}, chalice, human skull, and
            various herbs. There>s also mention of an <<{c:QItemElderSign,>>
            but you aren>t sure what that is.
            
            <i>I wonder if they actually have these already?</i> you think to
            yourself. 
        "
    END PAGE

    PAGE Page3
        PROLOG "Opening a portal doesn’t sound easy."

        BUTTON "Read the next page" AFTER "Tools"
    
        TEXT "
            The {c:QItemDagger}
        
            You flip the page. Here the book goes into detail about the
            {c:QItemDagger} needed to open the portal. You are surprised at how
            intricate the ritual is. There is also a section about blessing the
            {c:QItemDagger}, but when it gets to the actual blessing, it is
            written in a language you cannot read.

            {c:QItemElderSign}
        
            Once the portal has manifested, it is weak and unstable. An
            {c:QItemElderSign} is used to stabilize it. There is a picture of
            one here, so you at least know what it looks like now.

            Gain 1 {clue}.
        "
    END PAGE

    PAGE Page4
        PROLOG "
            Each tool seems to need special attention. This will require more
            study.
        "
        
        BUTTON "Read the next page" AFTER "Sacrifice"
    
        TEXT "
            The Sacrifice


            The next page delves into the importance of personal sacrifice.
            For this ritual, the sacrifice is small:  a few drops of your own
            blood. You shudder as you read about using your blood for the
            ritual.

            Suffer 1 Horror ({will} negates).
        "

	    IF journalReadPage4 THEN TEXT "
            The Sacrifice
        
            The next page delves into the importance of personal sacrifice.
            For this ritual, the required sacrifice is large. A chill runs down
            your spine as you realize that only a precious loved one is enough.
            <i>The boy from the journal,</i> you think to yourself. <i>He>s
            here somewhere and we>re going to find him.</i>
        
            The first time this is read, suffer 1 Horror ({will} negates), then
            gain 2 {clue} if you don>t go Insane.
        "
    END PAGE
    
    PAGE Page5
        PROLOG "
            Even more blood is required, and for a moment you wonder where
            it will come from. Then you remember the journal:  it>s you. This
            is the last page of the ritual.
        "

        BUTTON "Read the next page" AFTER "Commentary"

        TEXT "
            Commentary

            Finally, there is commentary and advice. One section discusses ley
            lines and how they allow you to draw more power for the ritual.
            Determining the preferred dates and times for the ritual is also
            discussed, with a full moon being the most important part.
        
            In the margin are notes about a place under the house that align
            with a ley line; there is also a list of years that would be good
            for the ritual, and specific dates that are the best. Today is on
            the list.
        "

        IF journalReadPage4 THEN TEXT "
            Commentary

            Finally, there is commentary and advice. One section discusses ley
            lines and how to use them draw more power for the ritual.
            Calculating the date and time for the ritual is also discussed,
            with a full moon being the most important.
        
            In the margin are notes about a place under the house that aligns
            with a ley line; there is also a list of years that would be good
            for the ritual, and specific dates that are the best. Today is on
            the list.

            <i>The boy must be under the house somewhere,</i> you think to
            yourself.
        "

        TRIGGER @FoundCellHoleViaJournal
    END PAGE
    
    EPILOG
        TEXT "
            <i>Maybe I need to explore a bit more to figure out what I need to
            do to stop this madness,</i> you think to yourself.
        "
    
        IF exploredTortureChamber THEN TEXT "
            Now you know where the ritual will be performed and what is needed.
            You must stop your uncle!
        "

        IF readJournalPage4 THEN TEXT "
            You cannot allow a boy to be sacrificed for this evil. You must
            find the artifacts before the townspeople do and, if you can,
            save the boy.
        "
    END EPILOG
END BOOK